cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or the error-rate table, please cite it.
title: >-
  MitoFeasible: a position-level feasibility map for mitochondrial
  variant calling from bulk RNA-seq
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Uysal
    given-names: Selahattin Alperen
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Medical Biology and Genetics, Ege University,
      School of Medicine, Izmir, Türkiye
repository-code: https://github.com/dralperenuysal/mitofeasible
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-15
keywords:
  - mitochondrial DNA
  - heteroplasmy
  - RNA-seq
  - NUMT
  - detection limit
  - variant calling
abstract: >-
  For each of the 16,569 rCRS positions, the lowest allele fraction at which a
  variant call from bulk RNA-seq is supported, derived from observed depth and a
  per-position error rate measured against the donors' own whole-genome data
  rather than assumed constant. The released tool applies that error rate to any
  chrM alignment, reading depth from the user's own BAM.
